WEBVTT

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:07.190
If anyone kills you, 
it will be either the Demon King…

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.690
or a human mage.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.000
You're there like the wind

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.630
Closing your eyes at sunset

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:36.260
I wonder what's on your mind

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.600
Beyond Journey's End

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:44.980
With your eyelids open

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.570
Your eyes shone like glass

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:56.320
It faintly smelled like a sunny day

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.460
Clear up the sky, let flowers bloom

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.670
Bloom and blame it on the sunny sky

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.050
Even the rain, when it stops

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:21.060
Will make you shine in the sunlight

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:26.440
Calm the stirring sounds in my heart

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:30.480
We go like the sunny wind

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.900
Go on and fly over that cloud

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.740
Further and further away

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.000
Episode 26: The Height of Magic

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.630
It blocked it.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.860
We expected this much.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:07.870
From here on out, 
it's a battle of attrition.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.730
They really are here. 
Methode's observations were correct.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.640
Try not to hold me back.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.240
I could say the same thing.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:31.490
Methode has determined the 
exact locations of the enemy.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.980
We can't beat them in a 
disorganized free-for-all.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:40.990
So we'll split up and stop the replicas 
before they gather here.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.620
We told each other our weakest matchups.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.880
Your own weakest matchup 
is your replica's as well.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:55.090
Our advantage is that we can 
communicate and work together.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.870
As long as we choose the right opponents,

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.940
we'll have the upper hand.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.070
Use numbers to deal with anyone 
we can't fight alone.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.660
It's funny how easy this is.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:50.180
If we do this, we can stop the replicas.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.640
Follow the plan.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.270
Got it. Good luck.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.540
There's one concern.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:13.530
I'm detecting fewer replicas than test-takers.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:19.540
In particular, I can't find 
Ms. Sense's replica, the greatest threat.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.660
You're right. I don't detect it either.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.300
We mustn't overlook Sense's replica.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.650
If she comes at us from behind, 
I won't be able to protect Fern.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.840
Worst case, we could both die.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:38.350
I haven't found Ms. Fern or 
Mr. Denken's replicas either.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.350
We'll have to search for them using 
more precise close-range detection.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:48.660
We wouldn't have had to worry 
about this if you weren't here.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:55.670
First-class mages must be able 
to overcome unfair adversity.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.920
And this doesn't even qualify as adversity.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:04.430
Besides, you can pass the test by simply 
watching your fellow test-takers' backs.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.540
Is this not a truly kind and peaceful test?

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.730
It's down,

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.960
but I can't say I enjoyed that.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.320
An ambush.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:35.870
Damned monstrosity.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.460
I don't recall neglecting 
my mana detection.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.670
Lawine, you should break your bottle, too.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:49.270
You're old enough to know when to quit.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.130
The test will be held again in three years.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:54.700
Damn it.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.680
I didn't make it in time.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:09.690
But my help wouldn't 
have changed the outcome.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:15.370
Even with its back turned, 
I still don't detect any openings.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:20.200
Either way, I must at least buy some time.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.840
You're Denken the Imperial Mage, right?

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.720
What's going on here?

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.510
Are you planning to fight that thing?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.220
I don't think you can beat it.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.730
I know.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:41.920
Denken, do we have to do this 
to conquer the dungeon?

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.090
Frieren is currently—

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:47.970
I didn't ask for an explanation. 
Is this necessary?

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.370
Yes.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:55.110
Then I'll defeat it.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:08:00.160
What are you talking about? 
Denken is the strongest one here.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.260
You couldn't even beat Wirbel.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:07.250
Yeah, that's not how this works.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:11.460
It's true that I'm an inexperienced 
third-class mage.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.580
I'm far weaker than Denken or Wirbel.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.410
But I think I can beat Sense.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.010
This is my specialty.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.770
Reelseiden, a spell that 
cuts almost anything.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:33.770
It cuts anything I think it can, 
and it can't cut anything I think it can't.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:39.150
So what? That spell is easily 
blocked by defensive magic.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:44.230
Oh, right. You watched my battle 
against Wirbel, didn't you, four-eyes?

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:49.120
Yeah, defensive magic is for blocking spells.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:52.620
It's hard for me to imagine cutting it.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.990
I see. Then either way, 
it won't work against Sense.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.530
Based only on what we can observe,

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:04.390
that hair has multiple layers of spells 
equal to defensive magic cast on it.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:07.980
I told you, that sort of logic doesn't matter.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.620
I'm talking about what I can visualize.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.660
Hey, wait.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.150
Huh.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:20.400
Figures. Sorganeil doesn't work.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.310
Well, a person's hair is part of their body.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.910
It's impossible to see all of her at once.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:30.930
Reelseiden.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:36.390
As I thought, Übel is fighting my replica.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:39.720
I already know who will win.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.240
It won't even be a real fight.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:47.610
It happened two years ago, 
during the second-class mage exam.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:53.660
Burg, a first-class mage, 
proctored the second test.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.620
He was so skilled in defensive magic

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:03.260
that he hadn't been injured once 
since becoming a first-class mage.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:06.300
“Immovable Cloak.”

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:08.850
The cloak he created using mana

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:13.710
was imbued with so many defensive spells 
that no magical attack could penetrate it.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:21.720
For the second test, the test-takers fired 
offensive magic against Burg and his cloak.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:26.390
It was a simple test. If they could make him 
take just one step back, they passed.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.800
Killing would result in disqualification,

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:36.180
and limits were imposed on offensive 
magic to protect the other test-takers.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.080
Next.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.440
No one was worried about Burg.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.850
Oh, I cut too deep.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.660
But he was easily killed

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:08.620
by a no-name girl who'd just recently 
become a third-class mage.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.640
This means I fail, right?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:17.080
I get it. Can I leave now?

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.030
I have just one question for you.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.360
Go ahead.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.840
How did you defeat his Immovable Cloak?

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:32.050
Have you ever sewn before, Sense?

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:34.380
No. Why do you ask?

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:37.700
You do seem like you come 
from a rich family.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:41.620
Or do you use magic to handle all that stuff?

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:48.140
I've actually never tried it myself, 
since I'm so clumsy.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.980
But I used to watch my sister 
sew all the time.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:07.340
When you cut cloth, you place the scissors 
against it like this and slide them through.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.820
It makes a really nice sound.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:17.330
I liked that sound.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.010
I don't see where you're going with this.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.650
I'm talking about visual imagination.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:28.720
Cloth can be cut. 
You expect to be able to cut it.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.490
She's out of her mind.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:36.980
It's true that anyone can 
imagine cutting cloth.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.860
Even an idiot can do that.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:43.010
But the world of magic isn't so simple.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:48.160
Magic can't create anything 
the caster can't visualize perfectly,

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:54.630
just as a diminutive ant can't imagine 
crushing a colossal dragon underfoot.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:13:00.730
Hardly any mages can imagine 
penetrating that cloak

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.690
and its impregnable magical defenses.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:11.270
Any mage can tell at a glance that 
that cloak blocks all magical attacks.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:13.890
Truly, any idiot can see that.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:21.600
As long as people are intelligent organisms, 
we cannot escape those fetters.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:26.400
But she trusted her own intuition instead.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:31.530
Despite understanding intellectually 
that it couldn't be cut,

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:35.700
she constructed a vision of cutting 
through the cloak according to her intuition.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:41.000
Her mind must not function like a person's.

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:43.960
It's practically a superpower.

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:47.710
Can I go now?

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:48.630
Yes.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:54.310
By the way, Sense, that's some pretty hair.

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:57.050
It must be tough to maintain.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:04.620
Perhaps I had already lost to her then.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.190
I can't imagine beating Übel.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.650
She's that bad a matchup for me.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:22.200
You all think too hard. 
Hair is something to be cut.

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:26.210
Maintaining my hair?

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.710
It's hell.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.280
I don't even want to think about it.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.180
Then you should cut it.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.470
I've got the picture.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:46.440
So you're buying time until 
Frieren defeats the Spiegel.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.150
Yes, that's right.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.840
We defeated three of the replicas.

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.990
That will make things easier.

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:57.360
In that case… Oh, my.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:01.900
Ms. Sense's replica was just destroyed.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.400
This mana…

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:07.370
It was the third-class mage Übel 
who defeated it.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.750
That's surprising.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.260
Is it? She was a pretty bad matchup for it.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:18.310
Battles between mages 
are like rock-paper-scissors.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.890
However, it is a complex and difficult game 
of rock-paper-scissors with infinite options.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:28.310
And you want as many options as possible, huh?

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:34.870
Sure. We'll help you slow down the replicas.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:38.610
I don't make a habit of trusting others,

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:41.870
but I'm not dumb enough to let a winning 
horse go when it's right in front of me.

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:49.140
Currently, there are two 
dangerous replicas we must stop.

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:55.010
I've determined the location of 
one of them: Mr. Denken's replica.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.630
I'd like you to handle that one.

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:04.900
Allow me to handle the other: 
Ms. Fern's replica.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:09.560
She's particularly skilled 
at concealing her mana.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:13.780
Unless we find her replica, 
it could ambush and kill someone.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.590
Can you really handle it alone?

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:20.270
Working alone will allow me to 
focus better on mana detection.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.790
She's pretty strong, you know.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.990
I have many talents.

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:27.550
When it comes to simply stopping 
someone, I'm quite skilled.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:35.440
Besides, I confirmed with the actual Ms. Fern
that my binding magic would work on her.

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.410
Take this.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.970
I can't move.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:40.030
All right. Let's go fight this thing.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:47.270
Übel, I'm not imagining this, am I?

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.320
Probably not.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.340
After all, you can't move, can you?

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.440
My replica is back in action.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:09.960
Will this keep going until 
that Spiegel thing is defeated?

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:13.890
It's a battle of attrition. 
This is getting fun.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.480
I couldn't agree more.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:19.380
Isn't it time for us to get out of here?

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.880
This opening won't do either.

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.890
Fern wouldn't notice it.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.020
I'll have to do it after all.

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:13.380
The vulnerability in my mana detection 
isn't enough to kill me.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.670
You're right.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:18.800
We could win with a bigger opening, though.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.200
You can win, right?

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:23.440
Then I'll create an opening.

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:26.280
Is that possible?

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:30.950
If I show an opening, then the replica 
will show an even greater one.

00:18:32.390 --> 00:18:34.700
But that would mean you…

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:38.470
If I focus on defense, it won't be fatal.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.260
Then what strategy should we use?

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:50.450
It's up to you. If you think 
we can win, then we can.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.140
How can you be so sure?

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:57.990
Because I underestimate you.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.260
I'm glad to hear that.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.990
That means we have a decent shot at winning.

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:05.230
It's still standing, but that's a fatal wound.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:07.220
I should finish it—

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:18.710
What happened? Was I attacked?

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.900
I don't sense any mana.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:26.200
I'm not recognizing this attack as a spell.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:30.670
Incredible, Ms. Frieren.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.210
So this is the height of magic.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:37.340
But this isn't like you.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.090
You've left yourself wide open.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:54.010
Well done, Fern.

00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:58.970
It's been about eighty years 
since I was last forced to use that.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:15.420
Now, let's end this.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.060
So it's over.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:32.010
I can't move another millimeter.

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:35.020
Wirbel, carry me.

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:38.170
You guys just can't stay on your feet, huh?

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:51.460
So this is the bottom of the 
Ruins of the King's Tomb.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:56.040
You've conquered the 
Ruins of the King's Tomb.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:22:02.530
Such a notable achievement makes you 
worthy of becoming first-class mages.

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:09.420
As promised, everyone who made it here 
has passed the second test.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:15.440
So, where are the ladies of the hour?

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:22.270
It's dark and scary in here!

00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:26.090
It's dark! It's scary!

00:22:25.520 --> 00:22:28.200
I guess I understand that feeling.

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:28.200
Dark! Scary!

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:34.410
The second test is now over.

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:39.710
It can even use healing magic.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:42.360
Impressive, right?

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:43.600
Uh, yeah.

00:22:47.330 --> 00:22:49.040
Who are you?

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:53.140
And I'm alright (I'll be alright)

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.060
Yeah, I hear you (I care about you)

00:22:56.060 --> 00:23:01.650
The wind teases this hair that's longer now

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:04.070
There's meaning in everything

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.070
Even the days that came to a halt

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:13.700
Now that I finally understand,
I've caught up to you

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:17.500
See, things that couldn't have been

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:20.370
Seen if it weren't for these eyes

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:25.050
Why? They begin to overflow

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:31.300
I won't ask to see you, so at least

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:37.060
Let me remember the past, just for today

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:43.060
So, if we were to meet again

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:48.940
No more hesitations, I'd choose the present

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.990
Anytime, anywhere, yah (wherever you are)

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:57.620
Anytime, anywhere (smile for me)

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.620
I'll be there (close your eyes,
and I'll always be there)

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.380
Even if there are no absolutes

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:06.420
I'm always aware of your thoughts

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:12.470
Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:19.390
I'm whispering our lullaby
for you to come back home

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:23.190
It's been with me ever since I was little.

00:24:20.510 --> 00:24:22.850
You were unlucky this time.

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:23.750
That's the spell Flamme taught you.

00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:25.230
I may seem fine, but I'm actually 
in a terrible mood right now.

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:24.870
You're in really rough shape.

00:24:24.870 --> 00:24:26.900
The third test will now begin.

00:24:25.230 --> 00:24:27.720
Fern, let's head back.

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:27.730
Just make fun of me like you always do.

00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:29.980
